{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>I.</b> The meaning is the help of HaShem, or an allusion to the prince of Persia, as written in the book of Daniel (Daniel 10:20)." "<b>And the hadorim.</b> The opposite of אישר, and some say from the root הדר, and the meaning is mountains, and it is either an adjective or a noun of action." "<b>Gates of bronze.</b> They are at the gates of the cities."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:04.626238780Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}